      "hints": [
        "Calculate the volume after 30 seconds: $V = 600 \\times 30 = 18000\\text{ cm}^3$.",
        "Solve $\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = 18000$ for $r$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the total volume of the spherical balloon after $30\\text{ seconds}$ of pumping:\n$$V = 600 \\times 30 = 18000\\text{ cm}^3$$",
        "Use the volume formula for a sphere $V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$ to solve for radius $r$:\n$$\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = 18000 \\implies r^3 = \\frac{18000 \\times 3}{4\\pi} = \\frac{13500}{\\pi} \\approx 4297.18$$\n$$r = \\sqrt[3]{4297.18} \\approx 16.257 \\approx 16.3\\text{ cm} \\quad (\\text{to 3 s.f.})$$"
      ],
